			<div class="content" id="post-content-4804956">
									

<p>Just an idea I thought of one day while asking myself a question: How would the Foundation react if there was a way to escape the Earth and the myriad of anomalies it holds? This is the result.<br />
EDIT: Chose a path. Updated Accordingly. Thanks Quadraginta for the advice!<br />
EDIT II: Redid my idea a bit in response to crit. Thanks Nagiros for the advice!<br />
EDIT III: Adding in what is contained within my third response from Nagiros due to positive feedback via PM (they currently have IRL commitments, and thus can't continue the crit)</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Sorrowful, Dramatic, and Emotional (with undertones of Mystery)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Standard format (with ACS)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> What if there was a gateway to Paradise that we could reach? What if the entry was free? What if only the Foundation knew about it?</p>
<p>Here are the Shores of Paradise, a temperate, peaceful beach full of docile fauna, beautiful flora, and a gateway to Paradise. This 'Paradise' is a small pocket dimension with similar features to the beach, except with multiple biomes. As a secondary effect, the whole thing exudes a calming aura that makes people more agreeable and kinder (stronger in the pocket dimension). Sounds great, and the entry's free! But what if people found out?</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Very small coastal town somewhere close to a small beach where the Paradise gateway appears, changes the beach entirely. A couple of people visit, are amazed, see the Paradise gateway and promptly enter it.<br />
The Foundation gets strange missing person reports from that town as well as sightings of flora and fauna never seen before on Earth and decides to investigate. They find the beach and the Paradise gateway, make up explanations for the missing people, amnesticize the population of what they saw recently, and cordon off the area for 'dangerous animals' or something similar. The Foundation has everything under control.<br />
But when <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/competitive-eschatology-hub">disaster</a> strikes, this paradisal pocket dimension goes from unimportant to a potential evacuation point. Unfortunately, there's only space for about 100&#160;000 people, so who stays and who goes?<br />
There'll be a couple of main characters with differing opinions on whether to use this or not. When Paradise is filled however, the gateway shuts, and chaos ensues. Turns out the gateway was simply a way for a primordial nature spirit to gain sacrifices to increase its power and spread, and suddenly a new godlike entity enters the already chaotic battlefield of Earth.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> While somewhat similar to <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-778">SCP-778</a>, this Paradise is in fact being freely offered and can be seen. I believe it is different enough from that SCP that it can be considered a completely seperate idea.<br />
More importantly, this concept plays with human corruption, greed, desperation, and selflessness. Sometimes, stopping the bad people is easier than stopping the good.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> See my responses for more detail.</p>
<p>Anyway, thanks for reading!</p>
</div>
